{"step_index":105,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-14T11:37:01Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"# FeedForward 🌱\n\n**Zero-Waste Food Intelligence & Circular Redistribution System**\n\nFeedForward is a full-stack platform built for **Hostels**, **Event Managements & Restaurants**, and **Waste Processing Officials (Biogas & Animal Feed)**. It tackles food overproduction at the source through precise predictive consumer selections and routes inevitable food scraps into productive circular loops.\n\n---\n\n## Key Features & Requirements Solved\n\n### 1. Multi-Partition Architecture\n- **Hosteller / Student Portal**:\n  - Live pre-meal notification of upcoming menus (Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner).\n  - Clear **RSVP**: Confirm 100% attendance (\"Yes, I will eat\" vs \"No, I'm skipping\").\n  - **Dietary Selection**: Pure Vegetarian vs Non-Vegetarian.\n  - **Exact Item Quantity Planning**: Specify exact quantities (e.g. 3 Idlis, 2 Chapattis, 1 Rice bowl, Curry).\n  - Generates a **Digital Canteen Entry Pass** with item allowances and verification status.\n\n### 2. Gamified Food Waste & Black Star Penalty System\n- **Hostel Turnstile & Tray Disposal Enforcement**:\n  - If a student RSVPs \"Yes\" but fails to enter the canteen (wasting cooked food prepared for them), or throws away excess plate food at the tray return, the supervisor issues a **Black Star ⭐**.\n  - **3 Black Star Threshold**: When a hosteller reaches **3 Black Stars**, an automatic fine of **₹100** is levied to their hostel fee balance.\n  - Interactive Black Star Meter displays real-time strikes, warning states, fine alerts, and one-click fine clearance/reset.\n\n### 3. Kitchen Head Chef Demand Dashboard\n- Live real-time aggregation of attendee commitments.\n- Breakdown of Veg vs Non-Veg diner totals.\n- Total food overproduction saved from students who explicitly opted out.\n- **Exact Itemized Cooking Prep Quota**: Tells the kitchen exactly how many pieces to cook (e.g., *255 Idlis, 180 Chapattis, 65 Rice bowls*), eliminating excess prep.\n\n### 4. Circular Waste Redistribution & Official Dispatches\n- Segregation at mess, canteen, and event dish return:\n  - 🐾 **Plate Food Scrap (Clean & Edible)**: Automatically diverted to **Animal Feed** (Animal Rescue Shelters & Cattle Farms).\n  - ⚡ **Spoiled / Unfit Food Waste**: Diverted to **Biogas Anaerobic Digesters** for clean biomethane gas and green electricity generation.\n- **Automated Official Alerts**:\n  - When spoiled waste is logged, an urgent notification alert is dispatched to **Biogas Management** officials with quantity (kg), facility source, and timestamp.\n  - Clean plate food logs trigger pickup notifications to Animal Shelter partners.\n  - Officials can track pickups from *Pending Pickup* → *Dispatched* → *Collected*.\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start (How to Run)\n\n### Prerequisites\n- Python 3.10+ (Installed on Windows)\n\n### 1. Direct Execution\nSimply run the included batch launcher or PowerShell script:\n```cmd\nrun.bat\n```\nor via PowerShell:\n```powershell\n.\\run.ps1\n```\n\nOr manually in terminal:\n```bash\npython -m pip install -r requirements.txt\npython -m uvicorn backend.app:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000 --reload\n```\n\n### 2. Open Application\nOpen your browser at:\n```\nhttp://localhost:8000/\n```\n\n---\n\n## Testing & Verification\nAll core backend flows (RSVP quantity selection, chef aggregate calculation, gatekeeper check-in, black star penalties with 3-star fine triggers, and biogas/animal feed dispatches) have automated tests:\n\nRun backend tests:\n```bash\npython tests/test_backend.py\n```\n\nExpected output:\n```\n--- Running FeedForward Backend Verification Tests ---\n[OK] test_get_meals PASSED\n[OK] test_student_rsvp_and_chef_demand PASSED: Chef prep sheet shows 10 Idlis, 7 Chapattis\n[OK] test_canteen_entry_verification PASSED\n[OK] test_black_star_and_fine_trigger PASSED: Reached 3 stars -> Fine levied Rs 100.0\n[OK] test_fine_notification PASSED\n[OK] test_fine_payment_and_star_reset PASSED: Black stars reset to 0 after clearance\n[OK] test_biogas_official_notification PASSED: Urgent alert received by Biogas official\n[OK] test_waste_analytics PASSED: Biogas diverted: 133.5 kg (66.75 kWh green energy), Animal Feed: 71.5 kg (178 animal meals)\n\n[SUCCESS] ALL BACKEND TEST CASES PASSED PERFECTLY!\n```\n\n---\n\n## Project Structure\n```\nfeedforward/\n├── backend/\n│   ├── app.py              # FastAPI server, REST APIs, WebSocket live synchronizer\n│   ├── database.py         # SQLite schema, migrations, initial seed records\n│   ├── models.py           # Pydantic request/response validation models\n│   └── feedforward.db      # Persistent SQLite database\n├── frontend/\n│   ├── index.html          # Modern Single Page Application entry shell\n│   ├── css/\n│   │   └── style.css       # Custom animations, star meters, and glassmorphism styling\n│   └── js/\n│       ├── api.js          # Client-side API wrapper\n│       ├── state.js        # Reactive state store & WebSocket synchronizer\n│       └── app.js          # UI controller & role-based partition views\n├── tests/\n│   └── test_backend.py     # Automated test suite\n├── requirements.txt        # Python pip dependencies\n├── run.bat                 # Windows CMD one-click launcher\n├── run.ps1                 # PowerShell launcher\n└── README.md\n```\n","Description":"Documentation for FeedForward application","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"c:\\Users\\srira\\OneDrive\\Documents\\feedforward\\README.md","toolAction":"Creating README.md","toolSummary":"Create project documentation"}}]}
